        "comments": [
          {
            "id": 4232295959,
            "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Prepay excess transcription before accepting its cost**\n\nFresh evidence in this head is the new `heard()` debt path: Google has already produced and billed the transcript when this line passes its actual token count to `#owe`, which can drive `paid` below zero and only then start an asynchronous `spend` reservation. The added test explicitly exercises a 58-token debt; if the bridge dies or the reservation is refused before the API acknowledges it, that cost is absent from the durable committed total and a replacement can reuse the apparent remainder. Keep a guaranteed reserve large enough that transcription cannot create debt, rather than topping it up after receipt.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L15-L15](https://github.com/davidelaverga/Sophia/blob/86e96e796414bac843d39be502be636be0cd4f49/AGENTS.md#L15-L15)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "apps/media-bridge/src/qualification.ts",
        "line": 331,
        "outdated": false,
        "comments": [
          {
            "id": 4235198833,
            "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Prepay unasked turns before accepting their output**\n\nIf the bridge process is killed after unsolicited output reaches `received()` but before the asynchronous `#unasked()` reservation lands, neither `settle()` nor the in-memory handover can run, so the billed generation is absent from the durable ledger and a restarted bridge can reuse that budget. This is distinct from orderly shutdown and same-process replacement: reserve an unasked-turn contingency durably before the provider can emit spontaneous output, rather than charging only after receipt.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L15-L15](https://github.com/davidelaverga/Sophia/blob/096dd030e57f92828168894de968c31f3864120c/AGENTS.md#L15-L15)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
